# Zolto Release Changelog

All notable changes to the Zolto Extended Document Language are documented here.
Format: [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/) | Versioning: [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/)

---

## [10.0.0] — 2026-07-26 (Phase 10)

### Added
- **Interactive Document Engine**: Safe, declarative block directives for `@form`, `@quiz`, `@deck`, `@poll`, `@tasks`, `@tabs`, `@accordion`, `@state`, and `@shared`.
- **Quiz Scoring Engine**: Pure functional scoring for MCQ, multi-choice, true/false, fill-in-the-blank, and matching questions.
- **Flashcard Deck Engine**: Shuffle, progress tracking, difficulty grouping, and tag filtering.
- **Poll Engine**: Vote tallying and percentage computation.
- **Accessibility & Security**: Auto-generated ARIA roles, labels, keyboard navigation focus rings, and zero-eval safety guarantees.

---

## [9.0.0] — 2026-07-26 (Phase 9)

### Added
- **Component System**: Named PascalCase components with default, typed (`: string`, `: number`, `: bool`, `: enum`), and required (`!`) props.
- **Slot System**: Named slots (`slot header`), default slots, slot fallbacks, and slot forwarding.
- **Templates**: Document pattern templates (`template`) with template inheritance (`extends`).
- **Macros**: Text, parameterized (`macro note(text)`), and inline macros with safe 20-level recursion caps.
- **Control Flow**: Conditional rendering (`if`/`elseif`/`else`) and loop iteration (`each items as item,index key expr`).
- **Component Registry**: Document-scoped, imported, and built-in pattern registry (`Card`, `StatCard`, `AlertBox`, etc.).

---

## [8.0.0] — 2026-07-26 (Phase 8)

### Added
- **Spatial Layout Engine**: Responsive `@layout`, `@grid`, `@flex`, `@stack`, `@canvas`, `@pages`, and `@presentation` deck directives.

---

## [7.0.1] — 2026-07-25 (Phase 7 Patch)

### Fixed
- Chart Engine negative value handling, zero-baseline rules, and pie chart 12 o'clock start position.

---

## [7.0.0] — 2026-07-25 (Phase 7)

### Added
- **Vector Graphics Engine**: Declarative `@vector` block syntax compiling to SVG with scene graphs, transforms, and Bezier paths.
